{"availability":"available","full":"LALI20006/ai-robustness-defence-lab","name":"ai-robustness-defence-lab","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T10:22:17Z","updated":"2026-10-08T08:57:27Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ai-robustness-defence-lab.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://ai-robustness-defence-lab.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:20:43.157Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T13:20:43.157Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T13:20:43.157Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:47.661Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:04:50.171Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T13:20:43.157Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A hands-on machine learning security lab built to evaluate how well malware and network intrusion detection models hold up against adversarial attacks, and how to defend them.","Most machine learning models trained on network traffic or malware datasets look great in validation—often scoring 95%+ accuracy. But in real-world cybersecurity, attackers do not send clean data. By making tiny, bounded tweaks to network packets or PE file header features without breaking functionality, attackers can cause standard classifiers to completely misclassify threats as benign traffic.","We built this lab as an interactive workbench to:"],"features":["Train standard cybersecurity classifiers on realistic tabular data.","Stress-test those models with controlled feature-space perturbations (simulated evasion attacks).","Measure the exact vulnerability (Attack Success Rate, Accuracy Degradation, and Prediction Flip Rate).","Apply defensive techniques (adversarial retraining, input bounds validation, voting ensembles) and see if they actually fix the problem.","Export clean, reproducible PDF reports with all comparison charts and confusion matrices."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LALI20006/ai-robustness-defence-lab/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"aa13ef2dbbc6576810cc10f4a6ed90b300f322f7863a3d56afe25ab874f9f458","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:15.124Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:15.124Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A hands-on machine learning security lab built to evaluate how well malware and network intrusion detection models hold up against adversarial attacks, and how to defend them.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LALI20006/ai-robustness-defence-lab/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign in or create a quick account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LALI20006/ai-robustness-defence-lab/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"aa13ef2dbbc6576810cc10f4a6ed90b300f322f7863a3d56afe25ab874f9f458","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LALI20006/ai-robustness-defence-lab/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:15.124Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T08:57:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LALI20006/ai-robustness-defence-lab/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:15.125Z","hash":"aa13ef2dbbc6576810cc10f4a6ed90b300f322f7863a3d56afe25ab874f9f458","originalBytes":7714,"storedBytes":7714,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:47.661Z","subjects":[],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"AI & machine learning","subjects":[],"evidence":[],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Simulation & physics","Automation & workflows","Apple","Science","Data & dashboards","Privacy & security"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://ai-robustness-defence-lab.vercel.app/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-17T16:14:39.289Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-17T16:14:39.289Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-17T16:14:39.289Z